From 0623fd39008727c1c5e81a58154d50bc8c2b21dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 20:33:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: Phase 2 native Reaper_Firmware.asp + fix the check
 path (never cfg_mnt/ASUS)

Field report: the update badge never fired and the firmware page's Check
still talked to ASUS. Root cause: with RTCONFIG_CFGSYNC=y the stock page's
detect_update() takes the cfg_sync branch (apply.cgi?action_mode=
firmware_check -> do_firmware_check -> cfg_mnt blob -> ASUS's servers), so
the Phase 1 reaper_webs_update.sh never ran from the GUI (only from the
opt-in watchdog path). Second Phase 1 defect: reaper_webs_note.sh wrote
/tmp/release_note.txt while the GUI's viewer (/release_note0.asp,
nvram_dump) reads release_note0.txt - and it bailed when called argless via
the plain start_release_note rc service.

Phase 2 (the backlog item): a Reaper-native firmware page replaces the
stock tab and surfaces what stock disables - one-click download + install:

- www/Reaper_Firmware.asp (NEW, reaper_native chrome): installed
  model/variant/version card (variant derived from EXTENDNO _noMCP stamp),
  update check driven directly via start_webs_update + webs_state_* polling,
  inline release note (release_note0.asp), Download-and-Install with
  progress (stock ej ajax_fwdl_percent.asp), scheduled-check toggle
  (firmware_check_enable via saveNvram), manual .pkgtb upload to the stock
  upgrade.cgi with XHR progress + liveness verdict, flash veil + wait-for-
  reboot -> login. All strings tokenized (RFWU_1..31 in all 25 dicts,
  English-seeded; translation pass owed).
- rom/webs_scripts/reaper_webs_upgrade.sh (NEW, installed as
  /usr/sbin/webs_upgrade.sh, runs via the generic webs_* rc fallback):
  host-pinned to the AM-Reaper GitHub, re-checks model (anchored at _3006 so
  GT-BE98 never matches GT-BE98_PRO) and MCP/noMCP variant on-box, refuses
  to flash without a manifest SHA-256, tmpfs space check, GNU wget with
  fwget_log progress, size + sha256sum verify, stock firmware_check applet,
  then the stock flash sequence (ejusb/stop_logger/stop_jffs2/
  restart_upgrade). Never auto-runs - user-initiated only.
- reaper_webs_update.sh: parse new manifest fields 5/6 ->
  webs_state_sha256/webs_state_size (older 4-field manifests still work;
  the page then falls back to notify-only).
- reaper_webs_note.sh: argless-tolerant (version from webs_state_info) and
  writes /tmp/release_note0.txt (+ legacy release_note.txt copy).
- Advanced_FirmwareUpgrade_Content.asp (kept as fallback page): both
  cfg_sync_support branches of detect_update()/detect_firmware() disabled
  (if(0 && ...)) so even the stock page checks via the Reaper manifest.
- menuTrees/menuTree.js: Administration -> Firmware Upgrade tab now loads
  Reaper_Firmware.asp; dashboard badge href follows.
- reaper_inject.c: Reaper_Firmware.asp registered in reaper_native[].

Manifest format (stage_release.ps1, lean repo):
PRODUCTID#VARIANT#VERSION#URL#SHA256#SIZE.

Validated: sh -n on all three scripts; page ASCII-clean, all tokens present,
no single-quoted tokens, node --check on the inline JS with EN dict
substitution; dicts 25/25 lockstep at 6294; reaper_langcheck (now also
scanning Reaper_USB/Analytics/Firmware) 0 breakers across 25 languages.
Metal owed: check/badge/note round-trip, one-click install on a published
release, manual upload path, noMCP cross-variant refusal.
