--- a/release/src/router/www/CZ.dict
+++ b/release/src/router/www/CZ.dict
@@ -6261,3 +6261,34 @@ RDST_60=Store only
 RDST_61=Store only - keep connection-health history on the router; nothing is sent off it.
 RDST_62=History is written to the storage location selected above.
 RDST_63=Selecting a mode other than Off enables the connection-health probe.
+RFWU_1=Installed Firmware
+RFWU_2=Updates
+RFWU_3=Check for Update
+RFWU_4=Checking the Reaper release channel...
+RFWU_5=Your firmware is up to date.
+RFWU_6=Update available
+RFWU_7=Update check failed. The router could not reach the release channel, or no release is published for this model and variant. Details: /tmp/webs_upgrade.log
+RFWU_8=Download and Install
+RFWU_9=Download and install this update? The router will download the image, verify its SHA-256 checksum, flash it, and reboot. Do not power off the router until it comes back online.
+RFWU_10=Downloading firmware
+RFWU_11=Verifying and flashing. The router is rebooting into the new firmware.
+RFWU_12=Download failed. Check the internet connection and try again. Details: /tmp/webs_upgrade.log
+RFWU_13=Image verification failed. The downloaded file was discarded and nothing was flashed.
+RFWU_14=Scheduled Check
+RFWU_15=Check the Reaper release channel once a day (around 2 AM) and show a dashboard notice when a new release is published. Nothing is ever downloaded or installed automatically.
+RFWU_16=Manual Upload
+RFWU_17=Flash a firmware image file from your computer. Use the image built for this exact model and variant.
+RFWU_18=Uploading image
+RFWU_19=Release Notes
+RFWU_20=Installed version
+RFWU_21=Base build
+RFWU_22=The published manifest predates checksum support, so one-click install is disabled for this release. Update manually once; later releases install from here.
+RFWU_23=The previous firmware remains in the standby partition, and the bootloader rescue mode can always reflash the router over Ethernet.
+RFWU_24=Variant
+RFWU_25=Not enough free memory to stage the download. Reboot the router and try again.
+RFWU_26=Do not power off or restart the router.
+RFWU_27=The router rejected the uploaded image. Nothing was flashed.
+RFWU_28=Waiting for the router to come back online...
+RFWU_29=Model
+RFWU_30=The selected file does not look like an image for this router (model or variant mismatch). Flash it anyway?
+RFWU_31=Upload and flash this image? The router will verify it, flash it, and reboot. Do not power off the router until it comes back online.
